# EAS Build reads this from the monorepo root. Replicates .gitignore.
#
# apps/mobile/ios/ is NEVER uploaded. It used to be un-ignored here so EAS would
# skip its remote widget prebuild — but the directory is gitignored, so what got
# uploaded was one machine's untracked local snapshot. That snapshot went stale
# (it sat at CFBundleVersion 40 while app.config.js said 43), and because EAS
# skips prebuild whenever a native project is present, the build number in
# app.config.js was silently ignored. Meanwhile the containerized recipe cloned
# committed state, where ios/ does not exist, and prebuilt fresh — so the two
# paths produced different binaries from the same commit.
#
# Now there is one path: EAS prebuilds server-side from committed config on every
# build. The widget-target bug that motivated the un-ignore is handled in config
# instead, by apps/mobile/plugins/withWidgetVersionSync.js.
node_modules/
.pnp.*
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo/
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
android/
ios/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
spikes/**/results/*.json
.powersync/
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
